      "title": "Diamond laser sensor reads magnetic fields far more precisely",
      "summary": "Fraunhofer IAF researchers built a laser-enhanced diamond quantum sensor that reaches 100% optical contrast, improving the balance between sensitivity and measurable range by up to 590 times versus the best earlier approaches. That matters because sensors have usually had to trade fine sensitivity against the range of fields they can read. It is still a lab demonstration, and it needs engineering work before it can be used in real instruments.",
